// Adversarial: Sympathy cluster heal BFS at stack 1 — Dense layout.
//
// Dense layout provides ~20 adjacent cells so every bolt impact triggers a
// multi-ring BFS heal cascade. At stack 1, cascade depth is 1 (ring-1 only);
// the adversarial risk is that the BFS snapshot races the death pipeline:
// if a cell's Dead marker is not yet applied when the snapshot is taken, the
// cell appears as a valid BFS target and receives a heal, then the death
// pipeline removes it. This can produce a HealDealt<Cell> referencing a
// despawned entity — a NaN or panic path.
//
// Physics enabled (no debug_setup disable) so real bolt bumps drive actual
// DamageDealt<Cell> messages that trigger the BFS. 1500 frames gives enough
// time for the bolt to work through the Dense cluster and expose ring-heal
// arithmetic on cells at various HP levels.
//
// Invariants:
//   BoltInBounds     — bolt must stay in field during BFS churn
//   NoNaN            — ring-attenuation arithmetic (amount * factor^N) must not NaN
//   HazardStackValid — Sympathy stacks must stay registered throughout
//   NoEntityLeaks    — every HealDealt<Cell> entity must clean up; no orphans
//   BreakerInBounds  — breaker must not escape bounds during run
(
    breaker: "Aegis",
    layout: "Dense",
    input: Scripted((
        actions: [],
    )),
    max_frames: 1500,
    disallowed_failures: [
        BoltInBounds,
        NoNaN,
        HazardStackValid,
        NoEntityLeaks,
        BreakerInBounds,
    ],
    allowed_failures: None,
    debug_setup: None,
    seed: 1117,
    frame_mutations: [
        (frame: 5, mutation: InjectHazardStack(kind_name: "Sympathy", stacks: 1)),
    ],
)
